# Small-batch decode launch reductions for Qwen3.5/MTP on sm86.
#

Kind: feature
What: use a row-split bf16 SiLU*up kernel up to 64 query tokens and pass strided
  q/k/v views through the GDN speculative recurrence instead of materialising
  reshape copies. Both keep the arithmetic and output dtype unchanged; fp16
  uses vLLM's stock activation op.
Upstream: ported from TheRealBluesun/HyperQwen-3090ti, patches 09 and 10
  (1199731 and a332c5e), adapted to the vLLM 0.31 tree after the HyperQwen
  series. Their RTX 3090 measurements were 24.13 -> 23.34 ms/step for the
  small SiLU kernel and 23.34 -> 23.06 ms/step for strided GDN q/k/v.
Cut-against: 0.31.0 with patches/series applied through qwen3_5-embed-uva.
Retires-when: vLLM stops launching one CTA per token for small SiLU batches,
  or the GDN spec path stops copying q/k/v before the recurrence.

